course: dictionary
lesson: 1950
title: Communicate: sharing ideas
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To communicate means to share ideas, feelings or information with someone else. You can do it by talking, writing, using signs or making gestures. «Animals communicate with sounds, smells and body movements» shows that communicating does not always need words.
explain: The word has a second meaning: to understand each other well. «They communicate well» means they understand each other easily. The clue is well, which tells you the meaning is about understanding, not only speaking.
explain: Look at the phrases that go with it: communicate with, communicate by and communicate clearly. «Communicate with» tells you who you share with, «communicate by» tells you how, and «communicate clearly» tells you how well. In maths you communicate your reasoning by explaining each step.
fact: To communicate means to share ideas, feelings or information.
fact: You can communicate by talking, writing, signs or gestures.
fact: «Animals communicate with sounds, smells and body movements», but not with words.
fact: Scientists are studying whale clicks and other animal sounds with computers.
fact: No animal has yet been shown to use a language like ours.
exercise: «Animals communicate with sounds, smells and body movements.» According to this sentence, which way do animals NOT communicate? | Smells | *Words, like ours | Body movements | Sounds
exercise: «They communicate well.» What does this mean? | *They understand each other well | They are talking very loudly | They share ideas but never understand each other | They are joined by a door
exercise: In maths, how do you communicate your reasoning? | By whispering the answer | *By explaining each step | By drawing a picture only | By copying a friend
test: Your teacher asks you to communicate your idea in writing. Which is a way to communicate? | Shutting the door | Forgetting it | *Writing it down | Hiding it
test: «The two rooms were communicating.» What does communicating mean here? | Empty | Very noisy | Far apart | *Joined by a door
exam: «Animals communicate with sounds, smells and body movements.» Which meaning of communicate fits this sentence best? | Fall asleep | Run away from danger | Tell lies to others | *Share information with others
